  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1146 PM CDT THU AUG 6 2026\n\nThis evening, Central Alabama remains in a weak upper flow area \nsouth of the main broad trough that extends out of a Central\nCanada low and down into the Mid MS River Valley. At the same\ntime, Alabama is situated between two ridges, one across the Four\nCorners and the other in the Western Atlantic off of the VA/NC \nCoast with only minor perturbations traversing the weak flow \nacross Central Alabama. This has resulted in typical summertime \ndiurnally enhanced convection, but that is also at times outflow \ndriven. By Monday, the Western Atlantic ridge flattens and \nretrogrades westward across the Northern Gulf Coast. The only \ndifference for Monday onward will be that of a slightly different\norientation of the better rain chances from shortwave activity, \nbut it would still be diurnally enhanced.\n\nAs for temperatures, readings do vary a degree or so here and\nthere over the next week with overall moisture remaining up. This\nwill result in max afternoon heat indices perhaps a couple of degrees\nhigher in spots. However, guidance continues to keep us below heat\nadvisory criteria for now. \n\n08",
